WEBVTT

1
00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.134
(BIRD SCREECHES)

2
00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:09.604
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

3
00:01:10.939 --> 00:01:13.173
(BEE BUZZING)

4
00:01:16.678 --> 00:01:18.680
(BIRD SONG IN DISTANCE)

5
00:03:23.938 --> 00:03:26.339
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

6
00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:28.643
(HORNS HONKING)

7
00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.574
(DOOR CREAKS)

8
00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.617
(UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES)

9
00:05:05.273 --> 00:05:06.941
Hey!

10
00:05:07.041 --> 00:05:08.375
Are you single?

11
00:05:09.677 --> 00:05:11.579
I'm a matchmaker at Adore.

12
00:05:11.679 --> 00:05:13.781
Please give me a call if
you want to meet somebody.

13
00:05:13.881 --> 00:05:16.083
We have a lot
of great matches for you.

14
00:05:16.984 --> 00:05:17.952
Talk soon.

15
00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:33.100
James, hi.

16
00:05:33.201 --> 00:05:34.769
Thanks for calling me back.

17
00:05:34.869 --> 00:05:37.839
Um, I just wanted to get some
feedback on your first date

18
00:05:37.939 --> 00:05:39.240
with my client Sophie.

19
00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:40.842
I'm actually on my way
to meet her right now...

20
00:05:40.942 --> 00:05:42.877
but I had a quick chat
with her this morning...

21
00:05:42.977 --> 00:05:45.445
and the headline is,
she had a great time

22
00:05:45.546 --> 00:05:47.447
and would love
to see you again.

23
00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.552
Hello? James?

24
00:05:51.652 --> 00:05:55.056
JAMES: <i>Yeah, I'd like to be</i>
<i>taken off the service.</i>

25
00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:57.925
May I ask why?

26
00:05:58.025 --> 00:05:59.627
JAMES: <i>I thought you were</i>
<i>going to set me up</i>

27
00:05:59.727 --> 00:06:02.630
<i>with high-quality women.</i>

28
00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:06.433
<i>I said: a fit woman in her 30s</i>
<i>with a nice smile.</i>

29
00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.870
<i>She's 40 and fat.</i>

30
00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.772
-She's 39.
<i>-39 is not 30s, that's 40.</i>

31
00:06:11.873 --> 00:06:15.042
<i>I would never swipe right</i>
<i>on a woman like that.</i>

32
00:06:16.978 --> 00:06:19.446
-I'm sorry you feel that way.
-(LINE DISCONNECTS)

33
00:06:19.981 --> 00:06:21.015
(LINE BEEPS)

34
00:06:32.159 --> 00:06:33.995
SOPHIE: <i>I'm so happy.</i>

35
00:06:34.095 --> 00:06:36.297
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

36
00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.232
You did it, Lucy.

37
00:06:38.332 --> 00:06:42.637
When you said that he's 47
and only makes 150K a year...

38
00:06:42.737 --> 00:06:47.108
I almost said no, but I'm
really happy I trusted you.

39
00:06:48.276 --> 00:06:49.543
I know it's only been one date

40
00:06:49.644 --> 00:06:51.979
and I need to
manage my expectations...

41
00:06:52.079 --> 00:06:56.050
but this is probably the best
first date I've ever had!

42
00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:59.921
Uh, Sophie, so I just got off
the phone with him.

43
00:07:00.021 --> 00:07:02.323
And he loved meeting you,

44
00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:04.392
he had a great time...

45
00:07:04.491 --> 00:07:06.127
But he doesn't feel like
the chemistry

46
00:07:06.227 --> 00:07:08.428
is there for him at this time.

47
00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.463
So.

48
00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.001
Onward and upward.

49
00:07:15.303 --> 00:07:17.805
He doesn't want a second date?

50
00:07:18.973 --> 00:07:19.974
No.

51
00:07:22.209 --> 00:07:24.245
He's balding.
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

52
00:07:24.345 --> 00:07:26.347
How fucking dare he?

53
00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:28.049
LUCY: Dating is a risk.

54
00:07:28.149 --> 00:07:32.019
You took a risk. It's brave.

55
00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:34.855
SOPHIE: Why did you set me up
with someone like that?

56
00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.726
He checked
a lot of our boxes...

57
00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.529
and you checked a lot of his.

58
00:07:42.229 --> 00:07:44.432
So, onwards and upwards.

59
00:07:44.532 --> 00:07:45.633
Let's talk about
your next match.

60
00:07:45.733 --> 00:07:47.435
I have an amazing guy for you.

61
00:07:47.535 --> 00:07:50.137
His name is Mark,
he's a doctor,

62
00:07:50.237 --> 00:07:51.372
he's very handsome...

63
00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:54.008
he has a full head of hair,
he's 48.

64
00:07:54.108 --> 00:07:56.110
SOPHIE: That's almost 50.

65
00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:57.545
He looks great for 48.

66
00:07:57.645 --> 00:08:00.514
He's very fit.
He looks like he's 40.

67
00:08:00.614 --> 00:08:03.150
-How tall?
-5'11".

68
00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:07.588
Is he actually 5'11" or is he
actually 5'9" and is lying?

69
00:08:07.688 --> 00:08:09.557
What's a couple of inches?

70
00:08:09.657 --> 00:08:12.259
SOPHIE: I don't want
to waste my time.

71
00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:15.029
I am not asking for a miracle.

72
00:08:15.129 --> 00:08:17.999
I'm just asking
for the bare minimum.

73
00:08:18.099 --> 00:08:20.401
I'm trying to settle.

74
00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:22.403
LUCY: Sophie.

75
00:08:22.503 --> 00:08:24.572
I know how it feels right now.

76
00:08:25.406 --> 00:08:27.208
But I promise you...

77
00:08:28.943 --> 00:08:31.846
you're going to marry
the love of your life.

78
00:08:32.813 --> 00:08:34.482
SOPHIE: I don't believe you.

79
00:08:34.582 --> 00:08:35.916
That's okay.

80
00:08:37.051 --> 00:08:38.285
I believe it.

81
00:08:40.254 --> 00:08:41.655
(HORNS HONKING IN DISTANCE)

82
00:08:46.627 --> 00:08:48.829
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

83
00:08:50.064 --> 00:08:52.066
(ALL CHEERING)

84
00:08:57.772 --> 00:09:01.175
Girl of the hour!

85
00:09:01.275 --> 00:09:02.743
Tonight, we're all gathered

86
00:09:02.843 --> 00:09:06.180
to celebrate
the most talented Lucy.

87
00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:09.750
One hell of a matchmaker
with razor-sharp instincts...

88
00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:13.888
and an eagle eye for chemistry
because this weekend...

89
00:09:13.988 --> 00:09:18.592
her client Charlotte B.
is getting married!

90
00:09:18.692 --> 00:09:20.394
(ALL CHEERING)

91
00:09:20.494 --> 00:09:23.998
Charlotte B.
is marrying Peter C.

92
00:09:24.665 --> 00:09:26.535
The Prince Charming

93
00:09:26.634 --> 00:09:29.970
Lucy matched her with
20 months ago.

94
00:09:30.071 --> 00:09:33.340
How many marriages are you
responsible for now, Lucy?

95
00:09:34.275 --> 00:09:35.376
Nine.

96
00:09:35.476 --> 00:09:38.679
(CHANTING) Lucy! Lucy! Lucy!

97
00:09:39.647 --> 00:09:42.583
Lucy, do a speech!

98
00:09:42.683 --> 00:09:46.887
(CHANTING) Speech! Speech!
Speech! Speech!

99
00:09:54.462 --> 00:09:55.696
Okay.

100
00:09:56.831 --> 00:09:59.600
My speech is...

101
00:10:00.434 --> 00:10:01.969
that if the girl asks for

102
00:10:02.069 --> 00:10:03.737
a 6-foot-tall
drink of water...

103
00:10:03.838 --> 00:10:07.208
in his 40s with a salary
over 500 grand

104
00:10:07.308 --> 00:10:10.177
and a... good hairline...

105
00:10:10.277 --> 00:10:11.513
(ALL LAUGHING)

106
00:10:11.612 --> 00:10:12.713
you deliver.

107
00:10:12.813 --> 00:10:14.348
(ALL CHEERING)

108
00:10:15.683 --> 00:10:17.485
How did it go
with Sophie L. today?

109
00:10:17.586 --> 00:10:20.254
It took our membership team
an hour to get her to renew.

110
00:10:20.688 --> 00:10:22.356
Hopeless.

111
00:10:22.456 --> 00:10:24.825
I'm afraid there's not
a single man in New York City

112
00:10:24.925 --> 00:10:26.327
that'll date this girl.

113
00:10:27.428 --> 00:10:28.896
What seems to be the issue?

114
00:10:28.996 --> 00:10:31.533
That's the thing. There is
nothing wrong with her.

115
00:10:31.632 --> 00:10:34.768
She's okay attractive...

116
00:10:34.869 --> 00:10:39.707
okay money, okay educated,
okay personality.

117
00:10:39.807 --> 00:10:43.043
There's just not
a standout quality.

118
00:10:43.144 --> 00:10:45.412
She's not competitive
in the mainstream market...

119
00:10:45.514 --> 00:10:47.516
and there is
no niche market for her.

120
00:10:47.616 --> 00:10:48.782
Exactly.

121
00:10:48.883 --> 00:10:50.251
And if there's
no specialty appeal...

122
00:10:50.351 --> 00:10:52.753
then there's no place
for her in any market.

123
00:10:52.853 --> 00:10:54.589
That is tough.

124
00:10:54.688 --> 00:10:57.725
And she's my
favorite client right now.

125
00:10:57.825 --> 00:10:59.793
I mean, she's entitled
like everyone,

126
00:10:59.894 --> 00:11:02.029
but she's sweet...

127
00:11:02.129 --> 00:11:06.635
and she's realistic,
she's not crazy.

128
00:11:06.734 --> 00:11:08.435
She's a nice girl.

129
00:11:10.204 --> 00:11:11.839
There's got to be
a guy out there

130
00:11:11.939 --> 00:11:14.141
who just wants a nice girl.

131
00:11:14.241 --> 00:11:15.876
What about Mark P.?

132
00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:17.612
He's okay.

133
00:11:17.711 --> 00:11:19.813
LUCY: I pitched him
to her already.

134
00:11:19.914 --> 00:11:22.651
She's afraid
he's not actually 5'11".

135
00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:23.951
And I'm like,
can we please not worry

136
00:11:24.051 --> 00:11:25.186
about a couple inches
right now?

137
00:11:25.286 --> 00:11:27.188
Because you're
about to die alone.

138
00:11:27.288 --> 00:11:28.422
(CHUCKLES)

139
00:11:28.523 --> 00:11:30.257
You know
there's a surgery for that.

140
00:11:31.492 --> 00:11:33.160
For dying alone?

141
00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:34.995
For getting taller.

142
00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.731
Up to six inches.

143
00:11:37.831 --> 00:11:40.034
You break your legs, and...

144
00:11:40.134 --> 00:11:43.837
extend it,
let the bone heal itself.

145
00:11:43.938 --> 00:11:46.207
That's a game changer.

146
00:11:46.307 --> 00:11:48.342
It costs like 200K.

147
00:11:48.442 --> 00:11:52.479
Six inches can double
a man's value in the market.

148
00:11:53.747 --> 00:11:54.982
If you can afford it,

149
00:11:55.082 --> 00:11:57.051
it's definitely
worth the investment.

150
00:11:57.686 --> 00:11:59.019
What's the saying?

151
00:11:59.119 --> 00:12:02.557
"You're not ugly,
you just don't have money."

152
00:12:02.657 --> 00:12:03.625
LUCY: Right.

153
00:12:03.724 --> 00:12:06.160
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

154
00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:08.295
Do you have a dress
picked out for the wedding?

155
00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:10.231
Yes.

156
00:12:10.864 --> 00:12:12.634
Are you going alone?

157
00:12:12.733 --> 00:12:13.834
Mm-hmm.

158
00:12:13.934 --> 00:12:16.504
Lucy M.:
The Eternal Bachelorette.

159
00:12:16.605 --> 00:12:18.272
A voluntary celibate.

160
00:12:18.372 --> 00:12:20.241
Do you want me to set you up
with someone?

161
00:12:20.341 --> 00:12:23.010
No, I'm gonna die alone.

162
00:12:23.744 --> 00:12:25.614
Or get a rich husband.

163
00:12:25.714 --> 00:12:27.348
Same thing.

164
00:12:27.448 --> 00:12:28.449
(LUCY CHUCKLES)

165
00:12:40.528 --> 00:12:42.530
(INDISTINCT CONVERSATION)

166
00:12:43.897 --> 00:12:45.099
HARRY: Hi, Charles.

167
00:12:46.033 --> 00:12:47.801
Good to see you. (KISSES)

168
00:12:47.901 --> 00:12:49.169
You look beautiful.

169
00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:52.172
Oh, my God,
look how big they are.

170
00:12:52.674 --> 00:12:53.874
Mom.

171
00:12:54.375 --> 00:12:55.876
Congratulations.

172
00:13:02.483 --> 00:13:03.851
Nice to see you.

173
00:13:05.687 --> 00:13:07.221
You look beautiful.

174
00:13:08.389 --> 00:13:10.024
Nice to see you again.

175
00:13:10.791 --> 00:13:13.127
Hi, Henry. Hi.

176
00:13:13.227 --> 00:13:15.229
PATRICIA: I have been
saying to everyone

177
00:13:15.329 --> 00:13:17.464
that Peter and Char
are my couple goals...

178
00:13:17.565 --> 00:13:18.799
and I need to find
my own Peter

179
00:13:18.899 --> 00:13:20.334
and you're responsible?

180
00:13:20.434 --> 00:13:23.470
Well, I'm how Charlotte
and Peter met, okay?

181
00:13:23.571 --> 00:13:24.773
But it's up to the client

182
00:13:24.872 --> 00:13:26.006
to build a strong enough
relationship...

183
00:13:26.106 --> 00:13:27.441
that leads to marriage.

184
00:13:27.542 --> 00:13:28.777
But how did you know that

185
00:13:28.876 --> 00:13:30.578
Peter would be
the perfect guy for Char?

186
00:13:30.679 --> 00:13:33.314
JAIME: Well, she can't tell,
it's her industry secret.

187
00:13:33.414 --> 00:13:36.350
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)
There are no industry secrets.

188
00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:38.620
We can always
meet our life partner

189
00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:41.221
out in the wild
or swiping on apps.

190
00:13:41.322 --> 00:13:44.358
But the happy ending
to a first date...

191
00:13:44.458 --> 00:13:45.993
is not the second date.

192
00:13:46.093 --> 00:13:48.697
It's changing
each other's diapers

193
00:13:48.797 --> 00:13:51.332
and burying each other.

194
00:13:51.432 --> 00:13:53.568
You're looking for
a nursing home partner

195
00:13:53.668 --> 00:13:55.069
and a grave buddy.

196
00:13:56.604 --> 00:13:59.206
Who our partner is...

197
00:13:59.306 --> 00:14:01.810
it determines
our whole life...

198
00:14:01.909 --> 00:14:03.911
and how we live.

199
00:14:04.011 --> 00:14:07.281
Not for one, two,
ten years, but...

200
00:14:08.683 --> 00:14:10.351
forever.

201
00:14:10.451 --> 00:14:12.520
Oh, my God. (CHUCKLES)

202
00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.756
I need you so badly.

203
00:14:14.855 --> 00:14:15.889
Yeah, I'm desperate.

204
00:14:15.989 --> 00:14:17.358
Can I give you my card?

205
00:14:17.458 --> 00:14:18.892
Of course.

206
00:14:18.992 --> 00:14:20.528
I'm going through a divorce,
but once it's over...

207
00:14:20.628 --> 00:14:22.863
I would really, really like
to give you a call.

208
00:14:22.963 --> 00:14:24.064
I'm so sorry to hear that.

209
00:14:24.164 --> 00:14:26.568
Lucy. She needs you.

210
00:14:29.269 --> 00:14:30.304
Excuse me.

211
00:14:35.909 --> 00:14:38.979
(FOOTSTEPS THUMPING IN UNISON)

212
00:14:54.461 --> 00:14:56.897
I just need five minutes
alone with her.

213
00:15:02.604 --> 00:15:03.605
(DOOR CLOSES)

214
00:15:15.182 --> 00:15:17.619
-Hi, Charlotte.
-Hey, Lucy.

215
00:15:19.219 --> 00:15:20.921
LUCY: How're you holding up?

216
00:15:21.723 --> 00:15:23.290
Not good. (CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

217
00:15:24.925 --> 00:15:25.959
What's going on?

218
00:15:26.059 --> 00:15:27.428
(CHARLOTTE SNIFFLES)

219
00:15:28.897 --> 00:15:30.497
What's going on...

220
00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:35.035
is that I am a modern woman.

221
00:15:35.135 --> 00:15:37.104
Like, I could've been
anything.

222
00:15:37.806 --> 00:15:39.106
Anything.

223
00:15:39.206 --> 00:15:42.242
But I chose to become...

224
00:15:43.477 --> 00:15:45.045
a bride.

225
00:15:46.648 --> 00:15:48.248
I chose this.

226
00:15:50.150 --> 00:15:51.820
It's not like
I'm getting married

227
00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.220
because I need to forge a...

228
00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:56.457
relationship
between two kingdoms.

229
00:15:56.558 --> 00:15:59.960
It's not like my family
needs a cow. (LAUGHS)

230
00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:03.263
I chose this.
I chose to marry a man.

231
00:16:03.832 --> 00:16:04.766
LUCY: Charlotte.

232
00:16:04.866 --> 00:16:07.201
Marriage is a business deal.

233
00:16:08.135 --> 00:16:09.938
And it always has been

234
00:16:10.037 --> 00:16:12.574
since the very first time
two people did it.

235
00:16:14.174 --> 00:16:18.078
You can always walk away
if the deal isn't good.

236
00:16:18.178 --> 00:16:20.347
And as the person
who introduced you to Peter,

237
00:16:20.447 --> 00:16:23.116
I will walk
right out of here with you.

238
00:16:24.652 --> 00:16:27.555
So tell me: do you not want
to get married today?

239
00:16:27.655 --> 00:16:29.624
I have to.

240
00:16:29.724 --> 00:16:32.059
-LUCY: Why?
-Bec... (SCOFFS)

241
00:16:32.159 --> 00:16:36.564
My parents spent
so much money on this wedding.

242
00:16:36.664 --> 00:16:38.232
We spent hundreds
of thousands of dollars...

243
00:16:38.332 --> 00:16:39.366
on this wedding just so that

244
00:16:39.466 --> 00:16:42.637
I could feel like
a fucking woman.

245
00:16:42.737 --> 00:16:43.972
LUCY: Why do you really,

246
00:16:44.071 --> 00:16:47.207
in the darkest,
ugliest part of yourself,

247
00:16:47.307 --> 00:16:49.009
want to marry Peter?

248
00:16:49.109 --> 00:16:50.077
(CHARLOTTE SIGHS)

249
00:16:50.177 --> 00:16:52.547
And I promise you...

250
00:16:52.647 --> 00:16:54.414
I have heard every reason

251
00:16:54.516 --> 00:16:57.384
why a person wants
to get married to someone.

252
00:16:57.484 --> 00:17:02.891
And none of them are shocking
or wrong or crazy to me.

253
00:17:02.991 --> 00:17:05.492
It will be a secret
between you and me.

254
00:17:09.196 --> 00:17:11.131
You promise it'll be a secret?

255
00:17:11.231 --> 00:17:12.432
LUCY: I promise.

256
00:17:13.668 --> 00:17:17.337
You cannot tell anyone.

257
00:17:17.437 --> 00:17:21.141
Not a soul. It is so awful.

258
00:17:23.477 --> 00:17:25.713
LUCY: I will take it
to my grave.

259
00:17:42.195 --> 00:17:45.399
He makes my sister jealous.

260
00:17:47.401 --> 00:17:49.269
She's never said that,
but I know it's true.

261
00:17:49.369 --> 00:17:51.238
She thinks he's better
than her husband.

