I don't hate you.

526
00:33:33.581 --> 00:33:34.582
You do.

527
00:33:35.650 --> 00:33:38.085
And it's not because
we're not in love.

528
00:33:39.319 --> 00:33:40.989
It's because we're broke.

529
00:33:42.724 --> 00:33:44.726
(ENGINE IDLING LOUDLY)

530
00:33:48.228 --> 00:33:50.464
(ENGINE SCREECHES)

531
00:34:05.613 --> 00:34:06.581
(DOOR OPENS)

532
00:34:10.718 --> 00:34:11.719
(DOOR CLOSES)

533
00:34:16.290 --> 00:34:17.592
You want to come up?

534
00:34:23.565 --> 00:34:24.566
Yes.

535
00:34:27.035 --> 00:34:28.235
But I shouldn't.

536
00:34:33.373 --> 00:34:34.776
Thanks for the ride.

537
00:34:37.545 --> 00:34:38.546
JOHN: Anytime.

538
00:34:43.718 --> 00:34:45.620
Invite me to your play.

539
00:34:46.453 --> 00:34:47.454
I will.

540
00:34:51.025 --> 00:34:52.225
(DOOR CREAKS)

541
00:34:53.126 --> 00:34:55.329
(ENGINE STARTS, SCREECHING)

542
00:35:04.973 --> 00:35:06.206
I'm just giving you feedback

543
00:35:06.306 --> 00:35:07.609
so you can
improve your performance...

544
00:35:07.709 --> 00:35:09.343
and I can start
getting better matches.

545
00:35:09.443 --> 00:35:11.411
I want to meet someone
who is a combination of all

546
00:35:11.512 --> 00:35:14.214
the different awesome parts
of the last four matches.

547
00:35:14.314 --> 00:35:16.918
Sophie's job
and education level,

548
00:35:17.018 --> 00:35:19.520
Emily's body and lifestyle,

549
00:35:19.621 --> 00:35:22.657
Piper's face
and sense of style...

550
00:35:22.757 --> 00:35:26.961
and Jane's hobbies
and taste in TV shows.

551
00:35:27.061 --> 00:35:30.297
Easy,
since I'm Dr. Frankenstein.

552
00:35:30.397 --> 00:35:31.599
(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)

553
00:35:33.433 --> 00:35:34.802
I'm turning 48 in a few months

554
00:35:34.902 --> 00:35:38.006
and I think I need
to meet someone more grown.

555
00:35:38.106 --> 00:35:39.373
Someone I can talk to,

556
00:35:39.473 --> 00:35:42.476
just a proper woman
who knows good music...

557
00:35:42.577 --> 00:35:46.213
has seen old movies,
things like that.

558
00:35:46.313 --> 00:35:49.117
My last couple girlfriends
were 21 and 24...

559
00:35:49.216 --> 00:35:52.252
and they were honestly
kind of immature.

560
00:35:52.352 --> 00:35:54.388
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)
I can imagine it might be

561
00:35:54.488 --> 00:35:58.458
a little hard to relate
to girls born in the 2000s.

562
00:35:58.559 --> 00:36:00.695
I have a really
special client,

563
00:36:00.795 --> 00:36:02.162
her name is Sophie...

564
00:36:02.262 --> 00:36:04.932
she's a highly
accomplished lawyer, she's 39.

565
00:36:05.933 --> 00:36:07.501
Um...

566
00:36:08.435 --> 00:36:12.073
I wasn't really thinking 30s.

567
00:36:12.172 --> 00:36:13.306
LUCY: So when you
said older...

568
00:36:13.407 --> 00:36:15.543
I meant more like 27, 28.

569
00:36:16.010 --> 00:36:17.244
LUCY: Ah.

570
00:36:17.344 --> 00:36:19.080
It gets really intense
and complicated

571
00:36:19.179 --> 00:36:20.148
with women in their 30s.

572
00:36:20.247 --> 00:36:22.150
They have
really high expectations

573
00:36:22.249 --> 00:36:24.118
and they tend to rush things
because I guess,

574
00:36:24.217 --> 00:36:26.486
their biological clock's
ticking.

575
00:36:27.855 --> 00:36:30.858
I have another really
beautiful client, she's 31--

576
00:36:30.958 --> 00:36:31.926
Uh.

577
00:36:33.226 --> 00:36:34.696
No.

578
00:36:34.796 --> 00:36:37.532
Someone... 27.

579
00:36:38.465 --> 00:36:40.333
Even 29 is pushing it.

580
00:36:40.434 --> 00:36:42.036
Trust me-- it's the best thing
for everyone.

581
00:36:42.136 --> 00:36:43.671
I genuinely get along
much better

582
00:36:43.771 --> 00:36:44.872
with girls in their 20s.

583
00:36:46.674 --> 00:36:49.443
I don't care what she's like
or how she lives...

584
00:36:49.544 --> 00:36:52.080
I just care that
she's my type physically.

585
00:36:52.180 --> 00:36:54.148
LUCY: What's
your type physically?

586
00:36:54.247 --> 00:36:55.415
Fit.

587
00:36:56.050 --> 00:36:57.250
LUCY: Just fit?

588
00:36:57.952 --> 00:37:00.320
Fit. Nothing over 20 BMI.

589
00:37:00.922 --> 00:37:02.289
Okay.

590
00:37:05.459 --> 00:37:08.596
Thank you for agreeing
to come on a date with me.

591
00:37:08.696 --> 00:37:09.997
LUCY: Well, I only
said yes to this

592
00:37:10.098 --> 00:37:11.331
so you'd realize
you're wrong...

593
00:37:11.431 --> 00:37:12.767
and you're not actually
interested in me.

594
00:37:12.867 --> 00:37:15.069
HARRY: My instincts
are usually right.

595
00:37:15.169 --> 00:37:16.336
You think that
you're more right

596
00:37:16.436 --> 00:37:17.872
about this
than a professional?

597
00:37:17.972 --> 00:37:21.042
Oh, sure, you're the expert,
but I trust my gut.

598
00:37:21.142 --> 00:37:24.212
LUCY: Okay. We'll see.

599
00:37:24.311 --> 00:37:26.246
You look really good today.

600
00:37:30.952 --> 00:37:32.186
Thanks.

601
00:37:32.285 --> 00:37:34.287
LUCY: <i>How many drinks</i>
<i>per week?</i>

602
00:37:34.387 --> 00:37:39.359
Depends, but like, 8? 10?
Work makes it hard not to.

603
00:37:39.459 --> 00:37:41.729
-Do you do drugs?
-Never.

604
00:37:43.231 --> 00:37:45.032
I do pot at parties.

605
00:37:45.133 --> 00:37:46.266
Me too.

606
00:37:46.366 --> 00:37:48.301
So not never.

607
00:37:49.170 --> 00:37:50.905
Hmm.

608
00:37:51.005 --> 00:37:53.508
What do you think is your
best physical feature?

609
00:37:55.109 --> 00:37:56.476
My eyes aren't bad.

610
00:38:04.585 --> 00:38:07.522
How did you end up doing
what you do?

611
00:38:07.622 --> 00:38:09.557
Both my parents
work in finance...

612
00:38:09.657 --> 00:38:10.758
and so does my brother,

613
00:38:10.858 --> 00:38:12.459
so I just kind of
ended up doing it.

614
00:38:12.560 --> 00:38:14.394
And we all work for
the firm my mother started.

615
00:38:15.963 --> 00:38:18.900
-It's a family business.
-Yeah, it's boring.

616
00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:20.168
Mm.

617
00:38:20.268 --> 00:38:22.003
How did you get into
doing what you do?

618
00:38:24.471 --> 00:38:28.375
It was the... first
and (CHUCKLES) only thing

619
00:38:28.475 --> 00:38:29.777
I was really good at.

620
00:38:31.512 --> 00:38:33.147
HARRY: <i>What else do you want</i>
<i>to know about me?</i>

621
00:38:33.247 --> 00:38:34.549
I bet your parents
never raised

622
00:38:34.649 --> 00:38:36.416
their voices at each other.

623
00:38:37.317 --> 00:38:38.519
I think almost never.

624
00:38:38.619 --> 00:38:40.521
Maybe they were
secretly fighting.

625
00:38:42.190 --> 00:38:43.958
Did they ever
fight about money?

626
00:38:44.859 --> 00:38:45.860
No.

627
00:38:46.894 --> 00:38:47.895
Makes sense.

628
00:38:49.096 --> 00:38:51.766
I think we emulate the way
our parents fight.

629
00:38:52.166 --> 00:38:53.634
Hmm.

630
00:38:53.734 --> 00:38:55.069
I see couples fighting
in the middle of the street

631
00:38:55.169 --> 00:38:56.704
in New York
and I don't get it.

632
00:38:56.804 --> 00:38:59.439
Aren't they embarrassed to do
that in front of people?

633
00:39:01.474 --> 00:39:03.945
I'm the type to fight
in the middle of the street.

634
00:39:04.879 --> 00:39:07.215
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

635
00:39:07.315 --> 00:39:08.616
Have you ever done that?

636
00:39:10.685 --> 00:39:12.854
-Never.
-(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

637
00:39:12.954 --> 00:39:14.421
SOPHIE: <i>Do you think</i>
<i>he will like me?</i>

638
00:39:14.522 --> 00:39:15.990
I think you will
really like him.

639
00:39:16.090 --> 00:39:18.726
<i>-Are you sure?</i>
-Stay open-minded. (LAUGHS)

640
00:39:18.826 --> 00:39:20.995
<i>-I'm so nervous.</i>
-All right.

641
00:39:21.095 --> 00:39:22.230
Okay, text me after

642
00:39:22.330 --> 00:39:23.598
-and I'll call you tomorrow.
<i>-Okay.</i>

643
00:39:23.698 --> 00:39:25.233
-Okay, talk soon, Sophie. Bye.
<i>-Bye.</i>

644
00:39:25.333 --> 00:39:26.567
-Hi.
-Hi.

645
00:39:26.667 --> 00:39:28.636
-Wow. Thank you.
-(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

646
00:39:29.270 --> 00:39:30.470
You're welcome.

647
00:39:32.073 --> 00:39:33.406
You okay?

648
00:39:33.507 --> 00:39:35.910
Yes. My client is going
on a date right now too.

649
00:39:36.010 --> 00:39:37.111
You seem nervous.

650
00:39:37.211 --> 00:39:38.579
I really want her
to like this guy.

651
00:39:38.679 --> 00:39:40.380
She's had, like,
10 bad dates in a row

652
00:39:40.480 --> 00:39:42.049
and I just need to deliver.

653
00:39:42.149 --> 00:39:43.383
Are you feeling guilty that

654
00:39:43.483 --> 00:39:45.385
you're about to go
on a good date?

655
00:39:46.187 --> 00:39:48.022
(LUCY CHUCKLES)

656
00:39:48.122 --> 00:39:50.324
(FAINT INDISTINCT CHATTER)

657
00:39:50.423 --> 00:39:51.726
LUCY: I don't know
if I like you

658
00:39:51.826 --> 00:39:54.362
or if I just like the places
you take me to.

659
00:39:54.461 --> 00:39:55.563
You like me?

660
00:39:55.663 --> 00:39:57.765
When did that happen?

661
00:39:57.865 --> 00:40:00.234
I think when I saw the way
you pick up the bill.

662
00:40:00.334 --> 00:40:01.535
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

663
00:40:01.636 --> 00:40:03.237
HARRY: I do it
really well, don't I?

664
00:40:03.337 --> 00:40:04.872
You do.

665
00:40:04.972 --> 00:40:07.141
Just one swift motion.

666
00:40:08.441 --> 00:40:11.145
No hesitation. No fear.

667
00:40:11.245 --> 00:40:14.081
HARRY: Well, I can afford it,
so why would I be scared?

668
00:40:15.349 --> 00:40:17.251
You're investing
a lot in me, huh?

669
00:40:17.351 --> 00:40:20.688
I just want our dates
to be romantic.

670
00:40:20.788 --> 00:40:24.525
How expensive a meal is
makes the date romantic?

671
00:40:25.159 --> 00:40:26.193
Doesn't it?

672
00:40:30.598 --> 00:40:33.466
When we first met...

673
00:40:33.567 --> 00:40:36.337
you said your job makes you
think like a mortician

674
00:40:36.436 --> 00:40:38.706
or an insurance claims
adjuster.

675
00:40:39.439 --> 00:40:41.108
How am I as a corpse?

676
00:40:42.310 --> 00:40:43.844
A good corpse.

677
00:40:44.745 --> 00:40:46.280
How about as a payout?

678
00:40:46.380 --> 00:40:48.049
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY)

679
00:40:48.149 --> 00:40:49.250
Couldn't ask for better.

680
00:40:49.350 --> 00:40:50.952
As a nursing home partner?

681
00:40:53.154 --> 00:40:54.555
A grave buddy?

682
00:41:01.262 --> 00:41:03.097
You can do better than me.

683
00:41:03.931 --> 00:41:05.533
Can I?

684
00:41:05.633 --> 00:41:07.935
You know how to do
the math, don't you?

685
00:41:10.638 --> 00:41:12.940
In my line of work...

686
00:41:13.040 --> 00:41:15.409
I meet hundreds of
highly desirable,

687
00:41:15.509 --> 00:41:16.911
high quality men...

688
00:41:17.011 --> 00:41:21.649
but you are what we call
in my industry "a unicorn."

689
00:41:21.749 --> 00:41:24.352
An impossible fantasy.

690
00:41:24.452 --> 00:41:25.953
Your brother
was a unicorn, too.

691
00:41:26.053 --> 00:41:29.190
The reason my clients cannot
lower their expectations...

692
00:41:29.290 --> 00:41:31.459
is because, against all odds,

693
00:41:31.559 --> 00:41:33.861
men like you
do actually exist.

694
00:41:33.961 --> 00:41:36.030
Well, I'm sure something
is wrong with me.

695
00:41:38.332 --> 00:41:39.900
You're perfect.

696
00:41:41.102 --> 00:41:43.037
You're smart.

697
00:41:43.137 --> 00:41:46.674
You have ideal income,
ideal education...

698
00:41:46.774 --> 00:41:49.744
ideal lifestyle,
ideal height...

699
00:41:49.844 --> 00:41:52.213
you're good-looking,
you have a great body,

700
00:41:52.313 --> 00:41:53.748
you're charming.

701
00:41:55.549 --> 00:41:58.619
You were born rich,
raised rich,

702
00:41:58.719 --> 00:42:00.287
you're still rich.

703
00:42:00.388 --> 00:42:03.057
You own a penthouse
in Tribeca.

704
00:42:03.157 --> 00:42:05.059
You can take a girl
to a restaurant like this

705
00:42:05.159 --> 00:42:09.897
and it's not even (LAUGHS)
like a special occasion.

706
00:42:09.997 --> 00:42:14.635
You don't have a drug habit
or a call girls habit.

707
00:42:14.735 --> 00:42:16.904
You even know
how to cut your hair,

708
00:42:17.004 --> 00:42:18.672
and how to dress.

709
00:42:18.773 --> 00:42:20.141
You have taste.

710
00:42:21.742 --> 00:42:26.547
You are a 10 out of 10
in every category.

711
00:42:26.647 --> 00:42:28.883
A complete package.

712
00:42:28.983 --> 00:42:32.686
So I don't know why you're
trying to throw it all away

713
00:42:32.787 --> 00:42:33.754
on someone like me.

714
00:42:33.854 --> 00:42:35.689
What's someone like you?

715
00:42:36.590 --> 00:42:38.926
Just a girl who works.

716
00:42:41.095 --> 00:42:43.831
I'm older than the women
you could be dating.

717
00:42:43.931 --> 00:42:47.601
Which means my looks
won't last as long.

718
00:42:47.701 --> 00:42:49.904
And I have fewer years
left to get pregnant.

719
00:42:50.004 --> 00:42:52.373
If you marry a 25-year-old,

720
00:42:52.473 --> 00:42:55.609
then in 10 years
she'll look like me.

721
00:42:55.709 --> 00:42:58.746
If you marry me, in 10 years
I'll look like my mother.

722
00:42:58.846 --> 00:43:00.681
What does
your mother look like?

723
00:43:00.781 --> 00:43:03.651
I was born poor, raised poor,

724
00:43:03.751 --> 00:43:06.687
and even though I work,
I have debt.

725
00:43:06.787 --> 00:43:10.191
I'm a college dropout
and a failed actress.

726
00:43:11.659 --> 00:43:13.961
I have no dowry.

727
00:43:14.061 --> 00:43:16.497
If anything,
I have a negative dowry.

728
00:43:16.597 --> 00:43:18.732
Do I look like I need a dowry?

729
00:43:19.934 --> 00:43:23.437
At the end of the day,
the math doesn't add up.

730
00:43:23.538 --> 00:43:27.374
Given your position
in the marketplace
and given mine,

731
00:43:28.309 --> 00:43:30.144
I'm not a girl you marry.

732
00:43:31.712 --> 00:43:34.415
I'm a girl that
you go home with once,

733
00:43:34.516 --> 00:43:36.383
and then never call again.

734
00:43:39.954 --> 00:43:40.955
So...

735
00:43:41.822 --> 00:43:44.058
what are you doing with me?

736
00:43:48.028 --> 00:43:49.531
You say you think I'm smart,

737
00:43:49.630 --> 00:43:51.765
but you're talking to me
like I'm a caveman.

738
00:43:54.802 --> 00:43:56.303
I wouldn't date you
if I didn't see value.

739
00:43:56.403 --> 00:43:57.572
I'm not like my brother.

740
00:43:57.671 --> 00:43:58.873
I'm not looking
for the nicest,

741
00:43:58.973 --> 00:44:01.342
prettiest rich girl
who likes me back.

742
00:44:05.179 --> 00:44:07.148
I'm looking for someone
who understands the game,

743
00:44:07.248 --> 00:44:08.716
how the world works.

744
00:44:10.217 --> 00:44:12.353
I'm looking for someone
I respect.

745
00:44:13.320 --> 00:44:14.421
And trust.

746
00:44:16.157 --> 00:44:18.159
Someone who knows
more than me.

747
00:44:20.794 --> 00:44:22.730
I don't want to date you
for your material assets...

748
00:44:22.830 --> 00:44:24.165
though I think
you're underselling them

749
00:44:24.265 --> 00:44:26.033
by a significant margin.

750
00:44:27.569 --> 00:44:29.136
Material assets are cheap,

751
00:44:30.404 --> 00:44:31.805
they don't last.

752
00:44:33.340 --> 00:44:36.977
I want to be with you
for your intangible assets.

753
00:44:37.945 --> 00:44:39.246
Those are good investments.

754
00:44:39.346 --> 00:44:41.348
They don't degrade.
They only get sharper.

755
00:44:44.018 --> 00:44:45.886
And, besides,
I have enough material assets

756
00:44:45.986 --> 00:44:47.421
for the both of us.

757
00:44:51.425 --> 00:44:52.726
I see a lot of potential here.

758
00:44:52.826 --> 00:44:54.228
I think you and I could make
great partners.

759
00:44:54.328 --> 00:44:55.896
I hope you agree.

760
00:45:02.604 --> 00:45:03.672
As for what I can
do for you...

761
00:45:03.771 --> 00:45:04.738
I think I'm the only guy
this rich

762
00:45:04.838 --> 00:45:06.407
you can actually stand.

763
00:45:09.578 --> 00:45:11.712
I don't like you
because you're rich.

764
00:45:11.812 --> 00:45:13.380
Then why do you like me?

765
00:45:17.818 --> 00:45:20.321
Because you make me
feel valuable.

766
00:45:27.795 --> 00:45:29.463
You are valuable.

767
00:45:31.600 --> 00:45:33.500
That's what I'm trying
to tell you.

768
00:45:38.138 --> 00:45:40.508
Do you want to see
each other more seriously?

769
00:45:50.951 --> 00:45:52.886
-(SENSUAL INDIE MUSIC PLAYING)
-(ELEVATOR DINGS)

770
00:46:44.071 --> 00:46:45.272
(HARRY MOANS SOFTLY)

771
00:47:22.343 --> 00:47:23.477
(LUCY LAUGHING)

772
00:47:24.646 --> 00:47:27.114
(PHONE VIBRATING)

773
00:47:34.088 --> 00:47:35.889
-(LINE RINGING)
-(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

774
00:47:39.527 --> 00:47:41.261
(LINE RINGING)

775
00:47:41.362 --> 00:47:43.531
VOICEMAIL: <i>Hi, you've reached</i>
<i>Lucy from Adore Matchmaking.</i>

776
00:47:43.631 --> 00:47:44.766
<i>Please leave a message</i>

777
00:47:44.865 --> 00:47:45.800
<i>and I'll call you back.</i>
<i>Thanks.</i>

778
00:47:45.899 --> 00:47:48.302
-(BEEPS)
-Hey, it's John.

779
00:47:50.037 --> 00:47:52.239
Okay. Just give me a call
when you get this.

780
00:47:52.339 --> 00:47:55.042
Just wanted
